<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virovitica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Virovitica is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drava">Drava</a> river and the Hungarian border, in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a>. A royal free town of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, it was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> from 1552 to 1684 and then became the seat of Virovitica County, which covered much of Slavonia in the 18th and 19th centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virovitica.jpg" alt="Virovitica" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roko Poljak · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dvorac_Peja%C4%8Devi%C4%87_Virovitica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
